From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:58:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpufreq: apple-soc: point the idle drop at the
 cluster's CPUs at init

The T8132 P-cluster idle drop never fired on the J604: with all four P
cores 94-100 % of the time in cpuidle's cluster state and idle_drop on,
the drop count stayed 0 and the idle P-CPU rail stayed at 2.36 W.

->init() set the per-CPU pointer the idle hooks use from
policy->related_cpus, which the cpufreq core fills only after ->init()
returns, so no CPU got one and both hooks returned at once. Use
policy->cpus, which ->init() has already set to the cluster's CPUs, also
on the error path.

Fixes: bb9efa6b57 ("cpufreq: apple-soc: drop the all-idle T8132 P cluster to its slowest state")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 0737976671a5dd7e2b036477990006c3bf838681)
---
 drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
index 90ce14c715..0562472ce3 100644
--- a/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
+++ b/drivers/cpufreq/apple-soc-cpufreq.c
@@ -1648,7 +1648,12 @@ static int apple_soc_cpufreq_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 		priv->idle_pstate = freq_table[0].driver_data;
 		priv->run_pstate = FIELD_GET(APPLE_DVFS_CMD_PS1,
 					     readq_relaxed(reg_base + APPLE_DVFS_CMD));
-		for_each_cpu(i, policy->related_cpus)
+		/*
+		 * policy->cpus, not related_cpus: the core fills related_cpus
+		 * only after ->init() returns. Here policy->cpus still holds
+		 * every CPU of the cluster, online or not.
+		 */
+		for_each_cpu(i, policy->cpus)
 			per_cpu(apple_idle_priv, i) = priv;
 	}
 	policy->driver_data = priv;
@@ -1688,7 +1693,7 @@ static int apple_soc_cpufreq_init(struct cpufreq_policy *policy)
 
 out_clear_policy:
 	if (info->idle_drop)
-		for_each_cpu(i, policy->related_cpus)
+		for_each_cpu(i, policy->cpus)
 			per_cpu(apple_idle_priv, i) = NULL;
 	if (freq_qos_request_active(&priv->unmanaged_cap))
 		freq_qos_remove_request(&priv->unmanaged_cap);
-- 
